                    ,.
          %h3#RelativeCohesion Relative cohesion
          %p
            We discuss the relation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth\infty Grpd
            to other
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          %h4#continuous_cohesion Continuous cohesion
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETop%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ETop∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Euclidean-topological ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of definition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
