              \.
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For standard references on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            see there.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth \infty Grpd
            is discussed in section 3.3 of
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (2013)
          %p following
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              \:
              %em Sheaves and homotopy theory
              (1998) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DuggerSheavesAndHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A discussion of smooth
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
            and the presentaton of the
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes – An
                = succeed "-Lie" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#FSS"}> web
              ).
          %p
            For references on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Chern-Weil theory in Smooth∞Grpd
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+smooth+principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on a smooth principal ∞-bundle
          %p
            The results on differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
            used above are in
          %ul
            %li#Blanc
              P. Blanc,
              %em Cohomologie différentiable et changement de groupes
              Astérisque, vol. 124-125 (1985), pp. 113-130.
          %p and
          %ul#Brylinski
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              %em Differentiable Cohomology of Gauge Groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0011069"}> arXiv
              )
          %p which parallels
          %ul
            %li#Segal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              %em Cohomology of topological groups
              , Symposia Mathematica, Vol IV (1970) (1986?) p. 377
          %p A review is in section 4 of
          %ul
            %li#SchommerPries
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
              ,
              %em A finite-dimensional String 2-group
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2483"}> arXiv:0911.2483
              )
          %p
            Classification of topological
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %ul
            %li#BaezStevenson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              %em The classifying space of a topological 2-group
              Algebraic Topology
              %p
                Abel Symposia, 2009, Volume 4, 1-31 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3843"}> arXiv:0801.3843
                )
          %p
            and the generalization to classification of smooth
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %ul
            %li#NikolausWaldorf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              %em Four Equivalent Versions of Non-Abelian Gerbes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.4815"}> arXiv:1103.4815
              )
          %p
            Further discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            on smooth
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#Carchedi15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Carchedi"}> David Carchedi
              ,
              %em On The Homotopy Type of Higher Orbifolds and Haefliger Classifying Spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1504.02394"}> arXiv:1504.02394
              )
          %p
            On smooth ∞-groupoids (called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"}> differentiable stacks
            ” there) and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+Oka+principle"} smooth Oka principle
          %ul
            %li#Clough21
